I believe the context for this issue is "dot child" (e.g. `.somekey`) as union/bracket child should allow more esoteric possibilities (e.g. `[" "]`). Also, it may be relevant to (so called, currently) recursive descent (e.g. `..somekey`).

For consensus on digits as first identifier character, [dot_notation_with_number](https://cburgmer.github.io/json-path-comparison/results/dot_notation_with_number.html) and especially [dot_notation_with_number_object](https://cburgmer.github.io/json-path-comparison/results/dot_notation_with_number_on_object.html) are relevant.

@remorhaz is currently investigating the use of identifier syntax as part of https://github.com/jsonpath-standard/internet-draft/pull/5 and may wish to comment.

